  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 220C, fan-forced (see Kitchen hack). Line an oven tray with baking paper. Cut the lemon into wedges. Finely chop the spring onion. Crush or finely chop 2 garlic cloves. Coarsely grate the cheese. Drain and rinse the lentils.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2478286/photos/large/108512_1-2d6d710ddcfc11a513ba1420fffca45e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook lentil filling: Heat 1 tbs olive oil in a medium frypan over medium-high heat. Cook the garlic, stirring, for 1 min or until fragrant. Add the lentils, spinach, half the tomato paste and half the cumin and coriander spice blend and cook, stirring, for 1-2 mins until the spinach is wilted. Remove the pan from the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2478287/photos/large/108512_2-0327a6e2427aa62a97b10eab7365c58b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Assemble gozleme: Put 1 pita on the lined tray and spread with the lentil filling. Scatter over the cheese, then sandwich with another pita, pressing down firmly.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2478288/photos/large/108512_3-eae5c1c769924fb2cbc0099c3760ddc3.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake gozleme: Brush the gozleme with 1 tbs olive oil and bake for 12-15 mins, turning halfway (use a spatula to carefully flip it over), until golden brown and the cheese is melted.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2478289/photos/large/108512_4-c0031f356f15bcb4b4350024061d0b1a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Cut the gozleme into wedges and divide among plates. Scatter over the spring onion and serve with the lemon wedges. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2478290/photos/large/108512_5-2760a5e92f8660a47eee58e74c65193d.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen hack: Don't feel like turning the oven on? Simply warm the assembled gozleme in a large frypan over medium-high heat, carefully turning when golden underneath, until the cheese is melted.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2478291/photos/large/108512_6-5ab302b43c0cb9340b90c80394f1dc35.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
